 ## Overview
-Post-Voxelization Modifiers are algorithms applied to a discrete voxel grid after the initial geometric conversion to correct artifacts, optimize storage, or adapt the data for specific rendering pipelines [G]. This family modifies existing voxel attributes (density, material, opacity) without re-evaluating the source geometry [G]. It encompasses interactive editing, LOD downsampling, porosity injection, surface thickening, and multi-volume compositing.
