 ### [Voxel Editing Tools](17731-voxel-editing-tools.md)
-Voxel Editing Tools provide interactive, post-voxelization modification of volumetric data, allowing users to surgically alter individual or grouped voxels for tasks such as surgical planning, artifact correction, or data abstraction. Unlike the parent family which often applies algorithmic, non-interactive transformations, this method relies on direct user input via a stylus or pointer to define local regions of influence. It distinguishes itself from siblings like [Avatar Head Data Variant Application](22734-avatar-head-data-variant-application.md) by focusing on arbitrary spatial manipulation (removal, transparency, recoloring) rather than variant-specific attribute mapping. Choose this method when direct user-driven local edits are required. See [Voxel Editing Tools](17731-voxel-editing-tools.md).
