 ### Porosity via Spatial Pseudo-Random Hash Drop-out
-A technique to introduce controlled void space into voxelized meshes, simulating porous materials or reducing voxel count for aesthetic or performant reasons [S2, unofficial].
-- **Mechanism**: Voxels are dropped (set to empty) based on a spatial pseudo-random hash function. The decision is deterministic for a given coordinate, ensuring consistency across updates [S2, unofficial].
-- **Parameter**: Controlled by a `porosity` float parameter, passed via CLI (`--porosity <FLOAT>`) or API (`MeshProcessor::voxelize`) [S2, unofficial].
-- **Usage**: Chosen when simulating materials like foam or rock, or when reducing voxel density for performance without altering the mesh geometry [S2, unofficial].
-- **Link**: See [VoxelGrid from Mesh (Fill Method)](1013-voxelgrid-from-mesh-fill-method.md) for the base generation method.
