 ### Opacify Modifier
-A correction step for rendering thin or zero-thickness geometry (such as meshes) that would otherwise appear dashed, aliased, or partially transparent during ray marching or cone marching [S3, unofficial].
-- **Mechanism**: Meshes are hollow; voxelization gives partly covered voxels; the modifier scales coverage up so grazed surfaces read as solid, effectively thickening the voxel representation of the surface [S3, unofficial].
-- **Parameter**: `Amount` (default 2.0f). Increasing this value prevents surface leakage but may cause inflation; decreasing it reduces inflation but may reveal transparency. It is not a substitute for sufficient voxel resolution [S3, unofficial].
-- **Usage**: Chosen when rendering wireframes, thin shells, or low-poly meshes where standard voxelization fails to produce a solid appearance [S3, unofficial].
-- **Link**: See [Voxel Volume Rendering](6488-voxel-volume-rendering.md) for the rendering context.
