 ### Gaussian Smearing for Interface Blurring
-A preprocessing step to simulate the blurring of interfaces between different materials (e.g., rock and fluid) caused by finite voxel resolution in X-ray imaging [S5].
-- **Mechanism**: Identify the interface between the rock matrix and fluid phases in the simulation volume. Apply a Gaussian filter to the interface region to smear the boundary, creating voxels that contain mixed material properties [S5].
